[{"category":"section","location":"contributing/#Documentation-Build","page":"Contributing","text":"To build these docs locally:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.activate(\"docs\")\nPkg.develop(PackageSpec(path=pwd()))\nPkg.instantiate()\n\nThen run:\n\njulia --project=docs docs/make.jl\n\nThe generated local site is written to docs/build/.","title":"Documentation Build"},{"category":"section","location":"examples/#Examples","page":"Examples","text":"This example constructs the Burnside Mackey functor for the cyclic group C2.\n\nusing GAP\nusing AbstractAlgebra\nusing MackeyFunctors\n\nC2 = GAP.Globals.CyclicGroup(2)\nsubs = Vector{GapObj}(GAP.Globals.AllSubgroups(C2))\ne = subs[1]\ng = GAP.Globals.GeneratorsOfGroup(C2)[1]\n\nvalues = IdDict{GapObj, Vector{Int64}}(\n    e => [0],\n    C2 => [0, 0],\n)\n\nrestrictions = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, C2) => [1 2],\n)\n\ntransfers = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, C2) => [0; 1;;],\n)\n\nconjugations = IdDict{Tuple{GapObj, GapObj}, Matrix{Int64}}(\n    (e, g) => [1;;],\n)\n\nM = MackeyFunctor(C2, values, restrictions, transfers, conjugations)\n\nFor interactive visualization data, use:\n\nvisualizer_data(M)\nvisualizer_json(M)","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"design/MackeyContexts/#Mackey-contexts","page":"Mackey Contexts","text":"One of our time-saving design choices is the idea of a MackeyContext, which precompiles relevant information about a finite group before working with Mackey functors for that group. The idea is to make the construction of a Mackey functor a two-step process: step 1 is to build the context, and then step 2 is to build a Mackey functor for the context. This allows us to avoid certain costly computations, for instance computing what the formulas for the double coset formulas should look like.\n\nDefinition Let Hle Kle G be subgroups of a group G. We say that the tuple (HK) is a cover (and we will denote this by Hlesssim K) if H is a proper subgroup of K, and if Hle L le K is a pair of subgroup inclusions, then either H=L or L=K.\n\nThe MackeyContext data type stores the following information about the group:\n\nthe group itself\na list of all subgroups of the group\na list of all the covers Hlessim K\na list of paths between two subgroups: for every tuple of subgroups (HK) with Hle K, we store a single sequence of covers H = H_0 lessim H_1 lessim cdots lessim H_n = K\na list of generators for the group\na matrix generatorLeftConjugationMatrix, whose rows are indexed by generators(?) of the group and whose columns are indexed by subgroups, and where the gHth entry is the index in the list of subgroups of the subgroup gHg^-1\na similar matrix generatorRightConjugationMatrix telling us how to find g^-1Hg for a generator g\na dictionary doubleCosetRepresentatives: the keys are triples of subgroups (JHK), with Jlessim H and Klessim H, and the values are a vector of DoubleCosetFormulaTerm types: these are tuples of generator words and subgroup indices, indended to help us locate J^x cap K.","title":"Mackey contexts"},{"category":"section","location":"installation/#Installation","page":"Installation","text":"From the package checkout:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.activate(\".\")\nPkg.instantiate()","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"design/MackeyFunctors/#Mackey-functors","page":"Mackey Functors","text":"","title":"Mackey functors"},{"category":"section","location":"manual/constructors/#Constructors","page":"Constructors","text":"tbd","title":"Constructors"},{"category":"section","location":"#MackeyFunctors.jl","page":"Home","text":"MackeyFunctors.jl provides tools for constructing Mackey functors for arbitrary finite groups G.","title":"MackeyFunctors.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"manual/data_types/#Data-types","page":"Basic data types","text":"Here we discuss the basic data types used in this package.\n\nmisc","title":"Data types"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.MackeyFunctor","page":"Basic data types","text":"MackeyFunctor(G)\n\ntodo\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.MackeyFunctor"},{"category":"type","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.MackeyContext","page":"Basic data types","text":"MackeyContext(G)\n\nPrecompute subgroup-lattice and double-coset data for a finite GAP group G. This front-loads the computational effort of aspects of the group and its subgroup lattice which will be used throughout verifying the axioms for any G-Mackey functor.\n\nThis method inputs a group G, and precomputes its list of subgroups, the list of covers (meaning proper subgroups Hle K where there are no intermediate subgroups), a list of generators for the group, and matrices for how these generators act via conjugation on the list of all subgroups.\n\nImportantly, the MackeyContext type also stores all the data needed to verify the double coset formula for an inputted Mackey functor. An important lemma is that the double coset formula can be checked along subgroups Jle H ge K where each inclusion is a cover. Given a triple of subgroups as above, we have\n\nH = coprod_x JxK\n\nand we store this in a dictionary as a vector of entries (J^xcap K x).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.MackeyContext"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.restriction","page":"Basic data types","text":"restriction(M,H,K)\n\ntodo\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.restriction"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.transfer","page":"Basic data types","text":"transfer(M,H,K)\n\ntodo\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.transfer"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.generator_relations","page":"Basic data types","text":"generator_relations(group)\ngenerator_relations(group, generators)\n\nReturn GAP's relators for a finite presentation of group on generators.\n\nEach relator is returned as a GeneratorWord, with the same (generator_index, exponent) convention.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.generator_relations"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_data","page":"Basic data types","text":"double_coset_representative_data(ctx, j, h, k)\ndouble_coset_representative_data(ctx, J, H, K)\n\nReturn representatives for J \\ H / K, where J < H and K < H are cover relations in ctx.\n\nEach representative is returned as (word, intersection_index), where intersection_index points to J^x intersected with K in ctx.subgroups for the represented group element x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_data"},{"category":"function","location":"manual/data_types/#MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_words","page":"Basic data types","text":"double_coset_representative_words(ctx, j, h, k)\ndouble_coset_representative_words(ctx, J, H, K)\n\nReturn only the generator words from double_coset_representative_data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"MackeyFunctors.double_coset_representative_words"}]
